2026-11-09T01:10:52.1066722Z   ok   without the Carnot derate the buffer collapses to the plain curve
2026-11-09T01:10:52.1067096Z   ok   the terminal credit repays a stored buffer kWh at the flow-derated COP the simulation charged to store it, less what the tank loses first
2026-11-09T01:10:52.1067274Z   ok   and at -5 C that haircut is small: winter storage is not discouraged
2026-11-09T01:10:52.1067549Z   ok   which is genuinely dearer than the plain curve the old code paid
